From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add monthly and yearly health summaries with steps and sleep

Gadgetbridge already records steps and sleep per day, but there is no period
overview: the dashboard and the charts show a day, a week or a running period,
and there is no place that answers "how much did I walk this month", "what is
my average day", "how well did I sleep" or "which days and nights were best".

This adds a Health summary screen with:
- a month/year switch, paging to the previous and next period, and a refresh;
- total steps, the average over the days that actually recorded steps (missing
  days are not counted as zero), the number of recorded days, and how many days
  met the step goal;
- a bar chart of steps per day for a month and per month for a year;
- a yearly month-by-month step list that opens the corresponding month;
- a daily step leaderboard, highest first and capped at ten days;
- average sleep duration, sleep score, efficiency and deep/REM shares, the
  number of recorded nights and the number of nights that met the sleep goal;
- a nightly sleep chart for a month and an average-sleep chart per month for a
  year, plus a monthly sleep breakdown that opens the corresponding month;
- a sleep-quality leaderboard, highest score first and by duration when a night
  has no score;
- empty and error states for both halves, plus English, Simplified Chinese and
  Traditional Chinese strings.

The activity data comes from DailyTotals, so it follows the same per-device
arithmetic as the existing charts. Sleep sessions are attributed to the day
they end on; a device score is preferred and the age-based estimate is used
only when it is enabled and the device has none. When several devices recorded
the same day or night, the largest total is used, so wearing two watches does
not double the summary.
